# Line endings. This repo is edited on WSL (LF) and on the lab's Windows
# machine (CRLF). Without a policy, every file anyone touches on the other OS
# shows up as a whole-file diff, which buries real changes and makes the
# shared-drive parity check useless.
#
# Policy: LF in the repository, native in the working tree. Windows editors
# get CRLF, WSL gets LF, and git stores one canonical form either way.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must be LF even on Windows -- a CRLF shebang line makes the
# interpreter fail with a confusing "bad interpreter" error.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Legacy Windows-authored code from the house_jobs/housing_wages merge. Kept
# byte-for-byte as imported rather than renormalised, so a future diff against
# whatever it came from still lines up.
docs/joint_house_jobs/** -text

# Binaries: never convert, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.mat  binary
*.docx binary
*.pptx binary
*.mp4  binary
